EFFO INFO FILES -- what the authors themselves declared==================================================================EFFO (the European Forum For OS-9) asked contributors to file a structured'Info' description with each submission: purpose, author, availability, andany conditions.  29 of them survive in the forum disks, and this is what theysay.  It is first-hand licence information, not our reading of the code.Two fields look alike and are not: $SOURCE-AVAILABILITY says whether theSOURCE can be had, while $AVAILABILITY -- "Public, Shareware, Commercial?" --is the one that speaks to redistribution, and $CONDITIONS qualifies it.Reading the first in place of the second makes every one of these lookunconditionally free.The full Info file for a program is in /dd/DOC/<program>/info_<program>wherever we shipped the program.------------------------------------------------------------------CONDITIONS THAT ARE NOT SIMPLY 'PUBLIC'------------------------------------------------------------------Read these before redistributing.  They are the authors' words.  space          May only be used under the conditions listed in the documentation (help file). The conditions prohibit use for military purposes. YOU MUST READ THE CONDITIONS BEFORE USING THIS PROGRAM!                   (copyright: (c) 1990 by L.Zeller)  disktest       no military use                   (copyright: by St.Paschedag)  hist           no military use                   (copyright: by H. Hoheisel)  rxmod/txmod    no military use                   (copyright: by W. Wittig)                   THESE NOW SHIP, in CMDS/COMMS.  If you redistribute this                   collection, that condition travels with them.  hexed          no military use                   (copyright: by H. Hoheisel-Zimmermann)  help           1. This Program may only be used for peaceful applications. I do                 NOT ALLOW using this program for anything that has to do with                 devel